[00:20.83]1. We really want to imitate our God,
[00:24.03]To be impartial, as we know he is.
[00:27.23]To save all sorts of people is his will;
[00:30.43]He welcomes all to come and to be his.
[00:33.91](Chorus)
[00:37.39]It’s the person, not the place;
[00:41.28]It’s the heart and not the face.
[00:46.02]God’s message to all people we extend.
[00:50.70]So because we really care,
[00:53.22]We keep preaching ev’rywhere:
[00:55.74]“All sorts of people can become God’s friend.”
[01:09.31]2. It doesn’t matter where they may be found
[01:13.69]Or what at first they might appear to be.
[01:18.75]What really counts is what they are at heart—
[01:23.91]The inner self, the one Jehovah sees.
[01:25.87](Chorus)
[01:27.84]It’s the person, not the place;
[01:29.80]It’s the heart and not the face.
[01:34.36]God’s message to all people we extend.
[01:39.40]So because we really care,
[01:41.84]We keep preaching ev’rywhere:
[01:44.28]“All sorts of people can become God’s friend.”
[01:57.88]3. Jehovah welcomes all who make the choice
[02:01.88]To leave the world and all its ways behind.
[02:06.88]This we have learned, and this we want to share,
[02:11.88]And so we preach to people of all kinds.
[02:14.88](Chorus)
[02:17.88]It’s the person, not the place;
[02:19.24]It’s the heart and not the face.
[02:22.74]God’s message to all people we extend.
[02:26.24]So because we really care,
[02:29.24]We keep preaching ev’rywhere:
[02:32.24]“All sorts of people can become God’s friend.”